Developed a high-performance Power BI reporting suite for a finance team to transition from manual Excel-based tracking to an automated, interactive dashboard. The solution provides a unified semantic layer for analyzing customer-level profitability, net interest margins, and credit risk across various banking products.

🛠️ Technical Highlights
Data Modeling: Engineered a robust star schema to handle millions in financing receivables and deposits across multiple dimensions (Customer, Account, RM, and Product).

Advanced DAX:

Time Intelligence: Implemented YOY, MTD, and YTD logic with dynamic axis scaling to compare current performance (Jan '26) against prior years.

Financial Logic: Calculated complex metrics including FTP (Funds Transfer Pricing), Net Interest Margin (NIM) per segment, and Expected Credit Loss (ECL) trends.

Advanced Visualizations:

Waterfall Charts: Deployed to visualize the bridge from Profit Income to Net Operating Income.

Matrix Logic: Utilized advanced matrix configurations with conditional formatting for Yield and Margin analysis.

Risk Gauges: Custom-scaled gauges for Credit Risk Rating and FCL stages.

📈 Business Insights Delivered
Operational Efficiency: Automated the end-to-end reporting workflow, eliminating manual data consolidation for sales and finance teams.

Profitability Tracking: Enabled real-time monitoring of a $13.2M Net Operating Income and $8.2M Net Profit, highlighting a 30.3% YOY growth.

Segment Performance: Identified high-performing segments, such as the 48.1% YOY growth in Fee Income.


